// C implementation limits (limits.h)
// 
// This module is signature-only.
// 
// Most limits are preprocessor macros in C (e.g. `INT_MAX`), not functions.
// In Fun, you use these identifiers directly after importing this module.
// 
// Import:
// - `imp std.c.limits;`
// 
// Integer limits
// - `CHAR_BIT`:
// - Bits in a byte.
// - `MB_LEN_MAX`:
// - Max bytes in a multibyte character.
// 
// Signed integer ranges
// - `SCHAR_MIN`, `SCHAR_MAX`
// - `SHRT_MIN`, `SHRT_MAX`
// - `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`
// - `LONG_MIN`, `LONG_MAX`
// - `LLONG_MIN`, `LLONG_MAX`
// - `CHAR_MIN`, `CHAR_MAX` (depends on whether `char` is signed)
// 
// Unsigned integer maxima
// - `UCHAR_MAX`
// - `USHRT_MAX`
// - `UINT_MAX`
// - `ULONG_MAX`
// - `ULLONG_MAX`
// 
// Size/pointer limits (sometimes provided via other headers)
// - `SIZE_MAX` (commonly from `stdint.h`/`stddef.h`, but often visible with limits)
// - `PTRDIFF_MIN`, `PTRDIFF_MAX` (commonly from `stdint.h`/`stddef.h`)
// 
// Notes
// - The Fun compiler performs best-effort typing for many of these macros as
// `num` so they can participate in arithmetic and comparisons.
// - Availability varies by platform and C library.
